  "plan": {
    "goal": "Size the PLINK binary .bed dataset and per-chromosome files for a GWAS cohort of 17104 samples and 9908332 variants.",
    "rationale": "The .bed binary format packs 2 bits per sample per variant, so total size = n_samples × n_variants / 4 / 1e6 MB. Per-chromosome size uses the same rule applied to the largest chromosome's variant count (173432). The number of per-chromosome files equals the number of chromosomes in the dataset; for a standard human GWAS this is 25 (22 autosomes + X + Y + MT), which must be confirmed from the .bim file.",
